        "content": "     1→[\n     2→  {\n     3→    \"title\": \"Anvil Reference Docs for AI Agents\",\n     4→    \"description\": \"Anvil community released reference repository for AI coding agents. GitHub repository anvil-llm-reference provides Anvil-specific context to help agents avoid rediscovery and improve coding accuracy.\",\n     5→    \"author\": \"Anvil Community\",\n     6→    \"source\": \"Platform\",\n     7→    \"url\": \"https://anvil.works/forum/t/anvil-reference-docs-for-ai-agents/25885\",\n     8→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-18\",\n     9→    \"topics\": [\n    10→      \"ai-agents\",\n    11→      \"coding-reference\",\n    12→      \"anvil\",\n    13→      \"documentation\",\n    14→      \"developer-tools\"\n    15→    ],\n    16→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    17→  },\n    18→  {\n    19→    \"title\": \"LLM Agents: The Complete Guide for 2026\",\n    20→    \"description\": \"TrueFoundry published comprehensive guide to LLM agents covering architecture, implementation patterns, and best practices for building agentic AI systems in 2026.\",\n    21→    \"author\": \"TrueFoundry\",\n    22→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    23→    \"url\": \"https://www.truefoundry.com/blog/llm-agents\",\n    24→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-18\",\n    25→    \"topics\": [\n    26→      \"llm-agents\",\n    27→      \"guide\",\n    28→      \"architecture\",\n    29→      \"implementation\",\n    30→      \"best-practices\"\n    31→    ],\n    32→    \"type\": \"tutorial\"\n    33→  },\n    34→  {\n    35→    \"title\": \"Project Think: Building the Next Generation of AI Agents on Cloudflare\",\n    36→    \"description\": \"Cloudflare introduced Project Think focused on running LLM-generated code safely with Dynamic Workers. Features Agent Readiness score to evaluate site preparedness for AI agents.\",\n    37→    \"author\": \"Cloudflare\",\n    38→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n    39→    \"url\": \"https://blog.cloudflare.com/project-think/\",\n    40→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-17\",\n    41→    \"topics\": [\n    42→      \"cloudflare\",\n    43→      \"llm-code-execution\",\n    44→      \"agent-safety\",\n    45→      \"dynamic-workers\",\n    46→      \"infrastructure\"\n    47→    ],\n    48→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    49→  },\n    50→  {\n    51→    \"title\": \"Governing Coding Agent Sprawl with Unity AI Gateway\",\n    52→    \"description\": \"Databricks released solutions for managing coding agent sprawl through Unity AI Gateway. Addresses governance challenges as enterprises deploy multiple AI coding agents.\",\n    53→    \"author\": \"Databricks\",\n    54→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n    55→    \"url\": \"https://www.databricks.com/blog/governing-coding-agent-sprawl-unity-ai-gateway\",\n    56→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-17\",\n    57→    \"topics\": [\n    58→      \"databricks\",\n    59→      \"ai-governance\",\n    60→      \"coding-agents\",\n    61→      \"enterprise\",\n    62→      \"management\"\n    63→    ],\n    64→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    65→  },\n    66→  {\n    67→    \"title\": \"A2UI v0.9: The New Standard for Portable, Framework-Agnostic UI\",\n    68→    \"description\": \"Google's A2UI Team introduced Agent SDK and shared web-core library enabling AI agents to drive cross-platform renderers. Advances portable UI for agentic applications.\",\n    69→    \"author\": \"Google A2UI Team\",\n    70→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n    71→    \"url\": \"https://developers.googleblog.com/a2ui-v0-9-generative-ui/\",\n    72→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-17\",\n    73→    \"topics\": [\n    74→      \"google\",\n    75→      \"ui-framework\",\n    76→      \"agent-sdk\",\n    77→      \"cross-platform\",\n    78→      \"generative-ui\"\n    79→    ],\n    80→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    81→  },\n    82→  {\n    83→    \"title\": \"Hacker News: Claude Opus 4.7 release discussion\",\n    84→    \"description\": \"Major discussion on Hacker News about Claude Opus 4.7 release with 1884 points and 1366 comments, showing significant community interest in Anthropic's latest model.\",\n    85→    \"author\": \"Hacker News Community\",\n    86→    \"source\": \"HN\",\n    87→    \"url\": \"https://news.ycombinator.com/\",\n    88→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-17\",\n    89→    \"topics\": [\n    90→      \"claude\",\n    91→      \"anthropic\",\n    92→      \"llms\",\n    93→      \"ai\",\n    94→      \"discussion\"\n    95→    ],\n    96→    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n    97→  },\n    98→  {\n    99→    \"title\": \"Hacker News: Qwen3.6-35B-A3B agentic coding release\",\n   100→    \"description\": \"Discussion about Qwen3.6-35B-A3B release with 1209 points and 496 comments. Community excited about open agentic coding model from Alibaba.\",\n   101→    \"author\": \"Hacker News Community\",\n   102→    \"source\": \"HN\",\n   103→    \"url\": \"https://news.ycombinator.com/\",\n   104→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-17\",\n   105→    \"topics\": [\n   106→      \"qwen\",\n   107→      \"agentic-coding\",\n   108→      \"llms\",\n   109→      \"ai\",\n   110→      \"open-source\"\n   111→    ],\n   112→    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n   113→  },\n   114→  {\n   115→    \"title\": \"ArXiv: The Agentification of Scientific Research\",\n   116→    \"description\": \"Paper exploring how AI agents are transforming scientific research from a physicist's perspective. Discusses implications for automated discovery and human-AI collaboration in research.\",\n   117→    \"author\": \"Xiao-Liang Qi\",\n   118→    \"source\": \"ArXiv\",\n   119→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.14718\",\n   120→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-17\",\n   121→    \"topics\": [\n   122→      \"agents\",\n   123→      \"scientific-research\",\n   124→      \"ai\",\n   125→      \"automation\"\n   126→    ],\n   127→    \"type\": \"paper\"\n   128→  },\n   129→  {\n   130→    \"title\": \"ArXiv: Layered Mutability in Self-Modifying Agents\",\n   131→    \"description\": \"Research on continuity and governance in persistent self-modifying agents. Addresses identity drift, persistent memory, runtime adaptation, and model editing challenges.\",\n   132→    \"author\": \"Krti Tallam\",\n   133→    \"source\": \"ArXiv\",\n   134→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.14717\",\n   135→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-17\",\n   136→    \"topics\": [\n   137→      \"agents\",\n   138→      \"ai-governance\",\n   139→      \"self-modifying\",\n   140→      \"identity\",\n   141→      \"safety\"\n   142→    ],\n   143→    \"type\": \"paper\"\n   144→  },\n   145→  {\n   146→    \"title\": \"ArXiv: Dr.RTL - Autonomous Agentic RTL Optimization\",\n   147→    \"description\": \"Autonomous agent for RTL (Register Transfer Level) optimization through tool-grounded self-improvement. Demonstrates agentic approaches to hardware design optimization.\",\n   148→    \"author\": \"Wenji Fang et al.\",\n   149→    \"source\": \"ArXiv\",\n   150→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.14989\",\n   151→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-17\",\n   152→    \"topics\": [\n   153→      \"agents\",\n   154→      \"hardware\",\n   155→      \"optimization\",\n   156→      \"autonomous\"\n   157→    ],\n   158→    \"type\": \"paper\"\n   159→  },\n   160→  {\n   161→    \"title\": \"ArXiv: Autogenesis - A Self-Evolving Agent Protocol\",\n   162→    \"description\": \"Research on protocols for self-evolving AI agents that can improve and modify themselves over time without human intervention.\",\n   163→    \"author\": \"Wentao Zhang\",\n   164→    \"source\": \"ArXiv\",\n   165→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.15034\",\n   166→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-17\",\n   167→    \"topics\": [\n   168→      \"agents\",\n   169→      \"self-evolution\",\n   170→      \"autonomous\",\n   171→      \"protocols\"\n   172→    ],\n   173→    \"type\": \"paper\"\n   174→  },\n   175→  {\n   176→    \"title\": \"ArXiv: OpenMobile - Open Mobile Agents Framework\",\n   177→    \"description\": \"Building open mobile agents with task and trajectory synthesis. Addresses challenges in mobile agent development and evaluation.\",\n   178→    \"author\": \"Kanzhi Cheng et al.\",\n   179→    \"source\": \"ArXiv\",\n   180→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.15093\",\n   181→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-17\",\n   182→    \"topics\": [\n   183→      \"mobile-agents\",\n   184→      \"framework\",\n   185→      \"task-synthesis\",\n   186→      \"evaluation\"\n   187→    ],\n   188→    \"type\": \"paper\"\n   189→  },\n   190→  {\n   191→    \"title\": \"ArXiv: Discovering Novel LLM Experts via Task-Capability Coevolution\",\n   192→    \"description\": \"ICLR 2026 paper on discovering specialized LLM experts through coevolutionary approaches. Presents method for identifying and leveraging model capabilities.\",\n   193→    \"author\": \"Andrew Dai et al.\",\n   194→    \"source\": \"ArXiv\",\n   195→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.14969\",\n   196→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-17\",\n   197→    \"topics\": [\n   198→      \"llms\",\n   199→      \"experts\",\n   200→      \"coevolution\",\n   201→      \"capabilities\",\n   202→      \"iclr2026\"\n   203→    ],\n   204→    \"type\": \"paper\"\n   205→  },\n   206→  {\n   207→    \"title\": \"Factory hits $1.5B valuation to build AI coding for enterprises\",\n   208→    \"description\": \"AI coding startup Factory reaches $1.5B valuation focusing on enterprise AI coding solutions, reflecting continued investor confidence in AI developer tools.\",\n   209→    \"author\": \"Marina Temkin\",\n   210→    \"source\": \"TechCrunch\",\n   211→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/17/factory-1-5b-valuation-ai-coding/\",\n   212→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-17\",\n   213→    \"topics\": [\n   214→      \"ai-coding\",\n   215→      \"startup\",\n   216→      \"enterprise\",\n   217→      \"valuation\"\n   218→    ],\n   219→    \"type\": \"news\"\n   220→  },\n   221→  {\n   222→    \"title\": \"llm-anthropic 0.25 released with Claude Opus 4.7 support\",\n   223→    \"description\": \"New model claude-opus-4.7 supports thinking_effort: xhigh. Added thinking_display and thinking_adaptive boolean options. Increased default max_tokens to maximum allowed for each model. No longer uses obsolete structured-outputs-2025-11-13 beta header.\",\n   224→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   225→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   226→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n   227→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-16\",\n   228→    \"topics\": [\n   229→      \"llm\",\n   230→      \"anthropic\",\n   231→      \"claude\",\n   232→      \"release\"\n   233→    ],\n   234→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   235→  },\n   236→  {\n   237→    \"title\": \"Qwen3.6-35B-A3B on my laptop drew me a better pelican than Claude Opus 4.7\",\n   238→    \"description\": \"Comparison of two big model releases from the same morning: Qwen3.6-35B-A3B from Alibaba and Claude Opus 4.7 from Anthropic, using the pelican riding a bicycle benchmark.\",\n   239→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   240→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   241→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n   242→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-16\",\n   243→    \"topics\": [\n   244→      \"ai\",\n   245→      \"generative-ai\",\n   246→      \"local-llms\",\n   247→      \"llms\",\n   248→      \"anthropic\",\n   249→      \"claude\",\n   250→      \"qwen\",\n   251→      \"llm-release\"\n   252→    ],\n   253→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n   254→  },\n   255→  {\n   256→    \"title\": \"datasette.io news preview tool built with Claude\",\n   257→    \"description\": \"Built a custom preview UI using claude.ai and Claude Artifacts for editing news.yaml file. Claude's ability to clone GitHub repos and examine content made this possible.\",\n   258→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   259→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   260→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n   261→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-16\",\n   262→    \"topics\": [\n   263→      \"vibe-coding\",\n   264→      \"claude\",\n   265→      \"tools\",\n   266→      \"datasette\"\n   267→    ],\n   268→    \"type\": \"tutorial\"\n   269→  },\n   270→  {\n   271→    \"title\": \"OpenAI takes aim at Anthropic with beefed-up Codex that gives it more power over your desktop\",\n   272→    \"description\": \"OpenAI releases enhanced Codex model with increased desktop control capabilities, directly competing with Anthropic's Claude models in the agentic coding space.\",\n   273→    \"author\": \"Lucas Ropek\",\n   274→    \"source\": \"TechCrunch\",\n   275→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/16/openai-codex-anthropic/\",\n   276→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-16\",\n   277→    \"topics\": [\n   278→      \"openai\",\n   279→      \"codex\",\n   280→      \"anthropic\",\n   281→      \"agentic-coding\",\n   282→      \"competition\"\n   283→    ],\n   284→    \"type\": \"news\"\n   285→  },\n   286→  {\n   287→    \"title\": \"InsightFinder raises $15M to help companies figure out where AI agents go wrong\",\n   288→    \"description\": \"Startup raises $15M for AI agent monitoring and debugging platform, addressing growing need for tools to understand and fix agent failures in production.\",\n   289→    \"author\": \"Ram Iyer\",\n   290→    \"source\": \"TechCrunch\",\n   291→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/16/insightfinder-series-a/\",\n   292→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-16\",\n   293→    \"topics\": [\n   294→      \"ai-agents\",\n   295→      \"monitoring\",\n   296→      \"debugging\",\n   297→      \"startup\",\n   298→      \"funding\"\n   299→    ],\n   300→    \"type\": \"news\"\n   301→  },\n   302→  {\n   303→    \"title\": \"Roblox's AI assistant gets new agentic tools to plan, build, and test games\",\n   304→    \"description\": \"Roblox enhances its AI assistant with agentic capabilities for game development, allowing it to plan, build, and test games autonomously.\",\n   305→    \"author\": \"Aisha Malik\",\n   306→    \"source\": \"TechCrunch\",\n   307→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/16/roblox-ai-assistant-agentic/\",\n   308→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-16\",\n   309→    \"topics\": [\n   310→      \"roblox\",\n   311→      \"ai-assistant\",\n   312→      \"agentic\",\n   313→      \"game-development\",\n   314→      \"tools\"\n   315→    ],\n   316→    \"type\": \"news\"\n   317→  },\n   318→  {\n   319→    \"title\": \"Canva's AI assistant can now call various tools to make designs for you\",\n   320→    \"description\": \"Canva enhances its AI assistant with tool-calling capabilities, allowing it to autonomously create designs by invoking various design tools.\",\n   321→    \"author\": \"Ivan Mehta\",\n   322→    \"source\": \"TechCrunch\",\n   323→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/16/canva-ai-assistant-tools/\",\n   324→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-16\",\n   325→    \"topics\": [\n   326→      \"canva\",\n   327→      \"ai-assistant\",\n   328→      \"tool-calling\",\n   329→      \"design\",\n   330→      \"automation\"\n   331→    ],\n   332→    \"type\": \"news\"\n   333→  },\n   334→  {\n   335→    \"title\": \"Antioch: Simulation startup wants to be the Cursor for physical AI\",\n   336→    \"description\": \"Antioch emerges from stealth with vision to become the Cursor of physical AI, providing simulation and development tools for robotics and embodied AI.\",\n   337→    \"author\": \"Tim Fernholz\",\n   338→    \"source\": \"TechCrunch\",\n   339→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/16/antioch-physical-ai-cursor/\",\n   340→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-16\",\n   341→    \"topics\": [\n   342→      \"simulation\",\n   343→      \"physical-ai\",\n   344→      \"robotics\",\n   345→      \"startup\",\n   346→      \"development-tools\"\n   347→    ],\n   348→    \"type\": \"news\"\n   349→  },\n   350→  {\n   351→    \"title\": \"datasette-export-database 0.3a1 released\",\n   352→    \"description\": \"Plugin upgrade needed after Datasette 1.0a27 no longer sets the ds_csrftoken cookie. Changes how the plugin uses signed URLs.\",\n   353→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   354→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   355→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n   356→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-15\",\n   357→    \"topics\": [\n   358→      \"datasette\",\n   359→      \"release\"\n   360→    ],\n   361→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   362→  },\n   363→  {\n   364→    \"title\": \"Datasette 1.0a27: CSRF protection modernized and RenameTableEvent added\",\n   365→    \"description\": \"Major changes: Replaced Django-style CSRF tokens with modern browser headers per Filippo Valsorda's research. New RenameTableEvent fires when tables are renamed during SQLite transactions, helping plugins react appropriately.\",\n   366→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   367→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   368→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n   369→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-15\",\n   370→    \"topics\": [\n   371→      \"datasette\",\n   372→      \"python\",\n   373→      \"security\",\n   374→      \"csrf\"\n   375→    ],\n   376→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   377→  },\n   378→  {\n   379→    \"title\": \"Gemini 3.1 Flash TTS released with surprising prompting requirements\",\n   380→    \"description\": \"Google released Gemini 3.1 Flash TTS, a text-to-speech model directed by prompts. The prompting guide requires elaborate context descriptions including character profiles, scene setting, and director's notes.\",\n   381→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   382→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   383→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n   384→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-15\",\n   385→    \"topics\": [\n   386→      \"google\",\n   387→      \"text-to-speech\",\n   388→      \"tools\",\n   389→      \"ai\",\n   390→      \"prompt-engineering\",\n   391→      \"generative-ai\",\n   392→      \"llms\",\n   393→      \"gemini\",\n   394→      \"llm-release\"\n   395→    ],\n   396→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   397→  },\n   398→  {\n   399→    \"title\": \"datasette-ports 0.3: Find all running Datasette instances\",\n   400→    \"description\": \"Tool update now shows working directory derived from each PID and full path to database files, making it easier to track what Datasette instances are running on a laptop.\",\n   401→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   402→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   403→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n   404→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-15\",\n   405→    \"topics\": [\n   406→      \"datasette\",\n   407→      \"tools\"\n   408→    ],\n   409→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   410→  },\n   411→  {\n   412→    \"title\": \"OpenAI updates its Agents SDK to help enterprises build safer, more capable agents\",\n   413→    \"description\": \"OpenAI releases updated Agents SDK with enhanced safety features and capabilities for enterprise agent development, reflecting maturation of agentic AI tooling.\",\n   414→    \"author\": \"Lucas Ropek\",\n   415→    \"source\": \"TechCrunch\",\n   416→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/15/openai-agents-sdk-update/\",\n   417→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-15\",\n   418→    \"topics\": [\n   419→      \"openai\",\n   420→      \"agents-sdk\",\n   421→      \"enterprise\",\n   422→      \"safety\",\n   423→      \"agentic-ai\"\n   424→    ],\n   425→    \"type\": \"news\"\n   426→  },\n   427→  {\n   428→    \"title\": \"Datasette replaces token-based CSRF with Sec-Fetch-Site header protection\",\n   429→    \"description\": \"Following Filippo Valsorda's research and Go 1.25's implementation, Datasette now uses modern browser headers instead of CSRF tokens. Removes need for hidden form inputs and simplifies API integration.\",\n   430→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   431→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   432→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n   433→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-14\",\n   434→    \"topics\": [\n   435→      \"csrf\",\n   436→      \"security\",\n   437→      \"datasette\",\n   438→      \"ai-assisted-programming\"\n   439→    ],\n   440→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   441→  },\n   442→  {\n   443→    \"title\": \"OpenAI announces GPT-5.4-Cyber model and Trusted Access program\",\n   444→    \"description\": \"OpenAI's answer to Claude Mythos: GPT-5.4-Cyber, a cyber-permissive variant for defensive cybersecurity. Also extending Trusted Access for Cyber program with ID verification for reduced friction access.\",\n   445→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   446→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   447→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n   448→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-14\",\n   449→    \"topics\": [\n   450→      \"security\",\n   451→      \"ai\",\n   452→      \"openai\",\n   453→      \"generative-ai\",\n   454→      \"llms\",\n   455→      \"anthropic\",\n   456→      \"ai-security-research\"\n   457→    ],\n   458→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n   459→  },\n   460→  {\n   461→    \"title\": \"Cybersecurity Looks Like Proof of Work Now\",\n   462→    \"description\": \"UK's AI Safety Institute report on Claude Mythos shows that more tokens spent equals better security results. This creates economic incentive to spend more on security reviews than attackers spend exploiting. Makes open source libraries more valuable as security costs can be shared.\",\n   463→    \"author\": \"Drew Breunig (via Simon Willison)\",\n   464→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   465→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n   466→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-14\",\n   467→    \"topics\": [\n   468→      \"open-source\",\n   469→      \"ai\",\n   470→      \"generative-ai\",\n   471→      \"llms\",\n   472→      \"vibe-coding\",\n   473→      \"ai-security-research\"\n   474→    ],\n   475→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n   476→  },\n   477→  {\n   478→    \"title\": \"Gitar raises $9M to use agents to secure code\",\n   479→    \"description\": \"Startup emerges from stealth with $9M funding for AI agent-based code security platform, applying agentic AI to vulnerability detection and remediation.\",\n   480→    \"author\": \"Lucas Ropek\",\n   481→    \"source\": \"TechCrunch\",\n   482→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/14/gitar-funding-agent-security/\",\n   483→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-14\",\n   484→    \"topics\": [\n   485→      \"security\",\n   486→      \"agents\",\n   487→      \"code-security\",\n   488→      \"startup\",\n   489→      \"funding\"\n   490→    ],\n   491→    \"type\": \"news\"\n   492→  },\n   493→  {\n   494→    \"title\": \"Emergent enters OpenClaw-like AI agent space from India\",\n   495→    \"description\": \"Indian startup Emergent launches in AI agent space, competing with OpenClaw by offering agentic coding capabilities from India perspective.\",\n   496→    \"author\": \"Jagmeet Singh\",\n   497→    \"source\": \"TechCrunch\",\n   498→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/14/emergent-india-openclaw-agents/\",\n   499→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-14\",\n   500→    \"topics\": [\n   501→      \"india\",\n   502→      \"startup\",\n   503→      \"agentic-coding\",\n   504→      \"openclaw\",\n   505→      \"international\"\n   506→    ],\n   507→    \"type\": \"news\"\n   508→  },\n   509→  {\n   510→    \"title\": \"Steve Yegge vs Google engineers on AI adoption\",\n   511→    \"description\": \"Steve Yegge claims Google has same AI adoption curve as John Deere (20% power users, 20% refusers, 60% using basic tools). Addy Osmani and Demis Hassabis dispute this, noting 40K SWEs use agentic coding weekly with custom tools.\",\n   512→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   513→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   514→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n   515→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-13\",\n   516→    \"topics\": [\n   517→      \"addy-osmani\",\n   518→      \"steve-yegge\",\n   519→      \"google\",\n   520→      \"generative-ai\",\n   521→      \"agentic-engineering\",\n   522→      \"ai\",\n   523→      \"llms\"\n   524→    ],\n   525→    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n   526→  },\n   527→  {\n   528→    \"title\": \"Exploring the new servo crate for Rust\",\n   529→    \"description\": \"After Servo v0.1.0 release, investigation shows it's now an embeddable browser engine with clear API. Built servo-shot CLI tool for taking screenshots. Compiling to WebAssembly not feasible due to threads and SpiderMonkey dependency.\",\n   530→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   531→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   532→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n   533→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-13\",\n   534→    \"topics\": [\n   535→      \"research\",\n   536→      \"browsers\",\n   537→      \"rust\",\n   538→      \"webassembly\",\n   539→      \"claude-code\",\n   540→      \"servo\"\n   541→    ],\n   542→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   543→  },\n   544→  {\n   545→    \"title\": \"Bryan Cantrill: LLMs lack the virtue of laziness\",\n   546→    \"description\": \"LLMs don't feel need to optimize for future time and will dump more onto layercake of garbage. Human laziness forces us to develop crisp abstractions because we don't want to waste time on clunky ones.\",\n   547→    \"author\": \"Bryan Cantrill (via Simon Willison)\",\n   548→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   549→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n   550→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-13\",\n   551→    \"topics\": [\n   552→      \"bryan-cantrill\",\n   553→      \"ai\",\n   554→      \"llms\",\n   555→      \"ai-assisted-programming\",\n   556→      \"generative-ai\"\n   557→    ],\n   558→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n   559→  },\n   560→  {\n   561→    \"title\": \"Transcribing audio with Gemma 4 E2B using MLX\",\n   562→    \"description\": \"Recipe for transcribing audio files on macOS using 10.28 GB Gemma 4 E2B model with MLX and mlx-vlm. Uses uv run with specific dependencies and can handle 14 second wav files.\",\n   563→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   564→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   565→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n   566→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-12\",\n   567→    \"topics\": [\n   568→      \"uv\",\n   569→      \"mlx\",\n   570→      \"ai\",\n   571→      \"gemma\",\n   572→      \"llms\",\n   573→      \"speech-to-text\",\n   574→      \"python\",\n   575→      \"generative-ai\"\n   576→    ],\n   577→    \"type\": \"tutorial\"\n   578→  },\n   579→  {\n   580→    \"title\": \"QuickJS Python Sandbox Investigation Report\",\n   581→    \"description\": \"Exploration of the quickjs Python package implementing an asyncio-compatible JavaScript sandbox with robust resource controls and seamless exposure of Python functions to JavaScript code.\",\n   582→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   583→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   584→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n   585→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-12\",\n   586→    \"topics\": [\n   587→      \"research\",\n   588→      \"javascript\",\n   589→      \"python\",\n   590→      \"sandbox\"\n   591→    ],\n   592→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   593→  },\n   594→  {\n   595→    \"title\": \"SQLite 3.53.0 released with ALTER TABLE enhancements\",\n   596→    \"description\": \"Major release includes ALTER TABLE can now add/remove NOT NULL and CHECK constraints, new json_array_insert() function, and significant CLI improvements with new Query Results Formatter library.\",\n   597→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   598→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   599→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n   600→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-11\",\n   601→    \"topics\": [\n   602→      \"sql\",\n   603→      \"sqlite\"\n   604→    ],\n   605→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   606→  },\n   607→  {\n   608→    \"title\": \"SQLite Query Result Formatter Demo playground\",\n   609→    \"description\": \"Interactive WebAssembly-based demonstration for trying out SQLite query result formatting in 20 different styles including box-drawing tables, CSV, JSON, HTML, and Markdown.\",\n   610→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   611→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   612→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n   613→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-11\",\n   614→    \"topics\": [\n   615→      \"tools\",\n   616→      \"sqlite\",\n   617→      \"webassembly\"\n   618→    ],\n   619→    \"type\": \"tool\"\n   620→  }\n   621→]\n   622→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
